  "description": "QIVREU crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H180 Fe6 Gd6 O60 P6. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2B (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd3B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1B (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe2B (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe3B (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Gd4? (Gd) has 0 O neighbors; Gd5? (Gd) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.322-4.092 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.27-120.78°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Fe6Gd6(μ3-O)2(O3PMe)6(O2CtBu)18(CO3)]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
